Using AND Operator - O(1) time and O(1) spaceThe idea is to use bit manipulation based on the observation that if n is a power of 2, then its binary representation has exactly one bit set to 1, and n-1 will have all bits to the right of that bit set to 1. Therefore, n & (n-1) will always be 0 for powers of 2. This provides an elegant one-line solution to check if a number is a power of 2 or not.
